sre-incident-bot: ALERT: embeddings-prod (us-west-2) latency spike detected. p90 > 1.5s since 12:40 UTC. Error rate low, timeouts trending up. Paging on-call.

jamie: I'm oncall, looking now. p95/p99 both climbing. Traces point to hotspots on model shard 'ggml-enc-2' and increased queue depth.

nina: FYI tagging runtime eng after triage if this looks like kernel regression.

leo: Support has 2 customers with slowed batch embedding jobs and 1 mobile search consumer reporting stale results. No full outages reported.

jamie: Hypothesis: KV cache eviction thrash + larger than usual batches causing request queuing on a few nodes. Live mitigation plan: 1) soft tenant-level rate shaping for bursty tenants, 2) shrink pool concurrency from 20 -> 10 temporarily, 3) disable streaming mirror workers that double-read KV and add load.

devx: Note: if you change server-side limits we should push an SDK advisory with recommended retry/backoff/idempotency patterns. I can draft.

jamie: Applying tenant token-bucket rate cap now via control plane.

jamie: curl -s -X POST "https://control.redwood.local/api/v1/ratelimits" -H "Authorization: Bearer $ONCALL_TOKEN" -d '{"tenant_id":"tenants/batch-heavy-1","rate":30,"burst":60}'

deploy-bot: rate-limit policy 723aef created and rolling to embed-prod us-west-2 (3 nodes). Deployed by jamie.

nina: Reducing concurrency on embed-prod pool in us-west-2:
rwctl set-concurrency embed-prod --region us-west-2 --concurrency 10

nina: Concurrency change accepted, observing p95 trending down after ~90s.

leo: Sent support note to affected customers: "Applying temporary rate shaping and reducing concurrency to improve tail latency. You may see longer queues for very large batch jobs." Customers prefer partial throttling over full downtime.

devx: Draft SDK guidance for bulletin: - Use Idempotency-Key for batch requests to avoid duplicates when retrying. - Retry on 429/503/ETIMEDOUT with exponential backoff + jitter. - Temporarily reduce client-side max concurrent requests (recommend 8).

devx: JS snippet to include in advisory:
// simple exponential backoff with jitter
async function retryWithBackoff(fn, attempts = 5) {
  for (let i = 0; i < attempts; i++) {
    try { return await fn(); } catch (err) {
      const retryable = ['429','503','ETIMEDOUT'].includes(err.code);
      if (!retryable || i === attempts - 1) throw err;
      const base = Math.min(1000 * 2 ** i, 10000);
      const jitter = Math.floor(Math.random() * 300);
      await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, base + jitter));
    }
  }
}

// Idempotency header example
fetch('/v1/embeddings', { method: 'POST', headers: { 'Idempotency-Key': uuid() } })

jamie: Also toggled streaming-mirror workers OFF for embed-prod in us-west-2 to cut duplicate KV reads.

deploy-bot: toggle streaming-mirror=OFF applied to embed-prod us-west-2.

nina: Observed ~30% p95 improvement after rate shaping + concurrency reduction + mirror toggle. p99 improved but still above target; continuing to monitor 15m window.

jamie: Handoff: I'm handing to nina at 13:00 UTC. If p99 doesn't approach <1s in 60m, next mitigations: 1) route subset of traffic to older model variant (quantized-1), 2) open hotfix for kernel selector to prefer lower-latency kernels for short sequences.

nina: Acknowledged. I'll post updates every 5 minutes. Escalate to runtime eng if plateau > 60m.

sre-incident-bot: Incident assigned to nina (sre). Severity: SEV-3. Postmortem owner: jamie.

nina: @product-ops please create a customer-facing status page entry: "Degraded embeddings latency in us-west-2; mitigation in progress."

product-ops: Will publish short entry in ~5m.

nina: 13:05 UTC check: p95 stable, p99 down ~18%, no error spike. Keeping tenant rate limits and concurrency reduction in place for at least 30m stable period before rolling back.

leo: Customers confirmed they prefer throttling. Support will keep notifying them on progress.

devx: Posted SDK advisory draft in #devx-incidents for review. Includes recommended backoff params, idempotency header usage, and suggestion to lower parallelism temporarily.

jamie: Good handoff. I'm entering rest mode. DM me if you need me.

nina: Continuing monitoring. If we see regression after rollback we'll open a hot patch with runtime team.

-- thread end --
